<title>FRANCE: France wine and spirits trade surplus widens.</title>
<headline>France wine and spirits trade surplus widens.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's trade surplus in wines and spirits widened in the first nine months of 1996 to 20.9 billion francs, up 4.6 percent over the year-earlier period, the French centre for external commerce CFCE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Wine exports rose 9.3 percent to 16.4 billion francs, more than offsetting a 3.7 percent fall in spirits exports to 8.2 billion francs and a 12.5 percent fall in vermouth exports to 116 million in the nine-month period.</p>
<p>Exports of wine, vermouth and spirits totalled 24.7 billion francs, up 4.4 percent, while imports were 3.8 billion, up 3.5 percent from the first nine months of 1995.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
